an10.104:4.8 | P: Catutthaṁ. | T: (none)

## an10.108
an10.108:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, doctors prescribe a purgative for eliminating illnesses stemming from disorders of bile, phlegm, and wind. | T: “Monks, doctors give a purgative for warding off diseases caused by bile, diseases caused by phlegm, diseases caused by the internal wind property.
an10.108:1.2 | S: There is such a purgative, I don’t deny it. | T: There is a purging there; I don’t say that there’s not,
an10.108:1.3 | S: But this kind of purgative sometimes works and sometimes fails. | T: but it sometimes succeeds and sometimes fails.
an10.108:2.1 | S: I will teach a noble purgative that works without fail. Relying on that purgative, sentient beings who are liable to rebirth, old age, and death, to sorrow, lamentation, pain, sadness, and distress are freed from all these things. | T: So I will teach you the noble purgative that always succeeds and never fails, a purgative whereby beings subject to birth are freed from birth; beings subject to aging are freed from aging; beings subject to death are freed from death; beings subject to sorrow, lamentation, pain, distress & despair are freed from sorrow, lamentation, pain, distress & despair.
an10.108:2.2 | S: Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” | T: Listen & pay close attention. I will speak.”
an10.108:2.3 | S: “Yes, sir,” they replied. | T: “As you say, lord,” the monks responded to him.
an10.108:2.4 | S: The Buddha said this: | T: The Blessed One said:
an10.108:3.1 | S: “And what is the noble purgative that works without fail? | T: “Now, what is the noble purgative that always succeeds and never fails, a purgative whereby beings subject to birth are freed from birth; beings subject to aging are freed from aging; beings subject to death are freed from death; beings subject to sorrow, lamentation, pain, distress & despair are freed from sorrow, lamentation, pain, distress & despair?
an10.108:4.1 | S: For one of right view, wrong view is purged. | T: “In one who has right view, wrong view is purged away,
an10.108:4.2 | S: And the many bad, unskillful qualities produced by wrong view are purged. | T: and the many evil, unskillful mental qualities that come into play in dependence on wrong view are purged away as well,
an10.108:4.3 | S: And because of right view, many skillful qualities are fully developed. | T: while the many skillful mental qualities that depend on right view go to the culmination of their development.
an10.108:5.1 | S: For one of right purpose, wrong purpose is purged. … | T: “In one who has right resolve, wrong resolve is purged away.…
an10.108:5.2 | S: For one of right speech, wrong speech is purged. … | T: “In one who has right speech, wrong speech is purged away.…
an10.108:5.3 | S: For one of right action, wrong action is purged. … | T: “In one who has right action, wrong action is purged away.…
an10.108:5.4 | S: For one of right livelihood, wrong livelihood is purged. … | T: “In one who has right livelihood, wrong livelihood is purged away.…
an10.108:5.5 | S: For one of right effort, wrong effort is purged. … | T: “In one who has right effort, wrong effort is purged away.…
an10.108:5.6 | S: For one of right mindfulness, wrong mindfulness is purged. … | T: “In one who has right mindfulness, wrong mindfulness is purged away.…
an10.108:5.7 | S: For one of right immersion, wrong immersion is purged. … | T: “In one who has right concentration, wrong concentration is purged away.…
an10.108:5.8 | S: For one of right knowledge, wrong knowledge is purged. … | T: “In one who has right knowledge, wrong knowledge is purged away.…
an10.108:6.1 | S: For one of right freedom, wrong freedom is purged. | T: “In one who has right release, wrong release is purged away,
an10.108:6.2 | S: And the many bad, unskillful qualities produced by wrong freedom are purged. | T: and the many evil, unskillful mental qualities that come into play in dependence on wrong release are purged away as well,
an10.108:6.3 | S: And because of right freedom, many skillful qualities are fully developed. | T: while the many skillful mental qualities that depend on right release go to the culmination of their development.
an10.108:6.4 | S: This is the noble purgative that works without fail. Relying on this purgative, sentient beings who are liable to rebirth, old age, and death, to sorrow, lamentation, pain, sadness, and distress are freed from all these things.” | T: “This, monks, is the noble purgative that always succeeds and never fails, a purgative whereby beings subject to birth are freed from birth; beings subject to aging are freed from aging; beings subject to death are freed from death; beings subject to sorrow, lamentation, pain, distress & despair are freed from sorrow, lamentation, pain, distress & despair.”
