## an10.103
an10.103:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, relying on the wrong way leads to failure, not success. | T: “From wrongness comes failure, not success.
an10.103:1.2 | S: And how does relying on the wrong way lead to failure, not success? | T: And how is it, monks, that from wrongness comes failure, not success?
an10.103:1.3 | S: Wrong view produces wrong purpose. Wrong purpose produces wrong speech. Wrong speech produces wrong action. Wrong action produces wrong livelihood. Wrong livelihood produces wrong effort. Wrong effort produces wrong mindfulness. Wrong mindfulness produces wrong immersion. Wrong immersion produces wrong knowledge. Wrong knowledge produces wrong freedom. | T: “In a person of wrong view, wrong resolve comes into being. In a person of wrong resolve, wrong speech. In a person of wrong speech, wrong action. In a person of wrong action, wrong livelihood. In a person of wrong livelihood, wrong effort. In a person of wrong effort, wrong mindfulness. In a person of wrong mindfulness, wrong concentration. In a person of wrong concentration, wrong knowledge. In a person of wrong knowledge, wrong release.
an10.103:1.4 | S: That’s how relying on the wrong way leads to failure, not success. | T: “This is how from wrongness comes failure, not success.
an10.103:2.1 | S: Relying on the right way leads to success, not failure. | T: “From rightness comes success, not failure.
an10.103:2.2 | S: And how does relying on the right way lead to success, not failure? | T: And how is it, monks, that from rightness comes success, not failure?
an10.103:2.3 | S: Right view produces right purpose. Right purpose produces right speech. Right speech produces right action. Right action produces right livelihood. Right livelihood produces right effort. Right effort produces right mindfulness. Right mindfulness produces right immersion. Right immersion produces right knowledge. Right knowledge produces right freedom. | T: “In a person of right view, right resolve comes into being. In a person of right resolve, right speech. In a person of right speech, right action. In a person of right action, right livelihood. In a person of right livelihood, right effort. In a person of right effort, right mindfulness. In a person of right mindfulness, right concentration. In a person of right concentration, right knowledge. In a person of right knowledge, right release.
an10.103:2.4 | S: That’s how relying on the right way leads to success, not failure.” | T: “This is how from rightness comes success, not failure.”
an10.103:2.5 | P: Tatiyaṁ. | T: (none)

## an10.104
an10.104:1.1 | S: “Mendicants, consider an individual who has wrong view, purpose, speech, action, livelihood, effort, mindfulness, immersion, knowledge, and freedom. | T: “When a person has wrong view, wrong resolve, wrong speech, wrong action, wrong livelihood, wrong effort, wrong mindfulness, wrong concentration, wrong knowledge, & wrong release,
an10.104:1.2 | S: Whatever bodily, verbal, or mental deeds they undertake in line with that view, their intentions, aims, wishes, and choices all lead to what is unlikable, undesirable, disagreeable, harmful, and suffering. | T: then whatever bodily deeds he undertakes in line with that view, whatever verbal deeds… whatever mental deeds he undertakes in line with that view, whatever intentions, whatever determinations, whatever vows, whatever fabrications, all lead to what is disagreeable, unpleasing, unappealing, unprofitable, & stressful.
an10.104:1.3 | S: Why is that? | T: Why is that?
an10.104:1.4 | S: Because their view is bad. | T: Because the view is evil.
an10.104:2.1 | S: Suppose a seed of neem, angled gourd, or bitter gourd was planted in moist earth. Whatever nutrients it takes up from the earth and water would lead to its bitter, acerbic, and unpleasant taste. | T: “Just as when a neem-tree seed, a bitter creeper seed, or a bitter melon seed is placed in moist soil, whatever nutriment it takes from the soil & the water, all conduces to its bitterness, acridity, & distastefulness.
an10.104:2.2 | S: Why is that? | T: Why is that?
an10.104:2.3 | S: Because the seed is bad. | T: Because the seed is evil.
an10.104:2.4 | S: In the same way, consider an individual who has wrong view, purpose, speech, action, livelihood, effort, mindfulness, immersion, knowledge, and freedom. | T: In the same way, when a person has wrong view… wrong release,
an10.104:2.5 | S: Whatever bodily, verbal, or mental deeds they undertake in line with that view, their intentions, aims, wishes, and choices all lead to what is unlikable, undesirable, disagreeable, harmful, and suffering. | T: then whatever bodily deeds he undertakes in line with that view, whatever verbal deeds… whatever mental deeds he undertakes in line with that view, whatever intentions, whatever determinations, whatever vows, whatever fabrications, all lead to what is disagreeable, unpleasing, unappealing, unprofitable, & stressful.
an10.104:2.6 | S: Why is that? | T: Why is that?
an10.104:2.7 | S: Because their view is bad. | T: Because the view is evil.
an10.104:3.1 | S: Consider an individual who has right view, purpose, speech, action, livelihood, effort, mindfulness, immersion, knowledge, and freedom. Whatever bodily, verbal, or mental deeds they undertake in line with that view, their intentions, aims, wishes, and choices all lead to what is likable, desirable, agreeable, beneficial, and pleasant. | T: “When a person has right view, right resolve, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, right concentration, right knowledge, & right release, then whatever bodily deeds he undertakes in line with that view, whatever verbal deeds… whatever mental deeds he undertakes in line with that view, whatever intentions, whatever vows, whatever determinations, whatever fabrications, all lead to what is agreeable, pleasing, charming, profitable, & easeful.
an10.104:3.2 | S: Why is that? | T: Why is that?
