an10.104:4.2 | S: Why is that? | T: Why is that?
an10.104:4.3 | S: Because the seed is good. | T: Because the seed is auspicious.
an10.104:4.4 | S: In the same way, consider an individual who has right view, purpose, speech, action, livelihood, effort, mindfulness, immersion, knowledge, and freedom. | T: In the same way, when a person has right view… right release,
an10.104:4.5 | S: Whatever bodily, verbal, or mental deeds they undertake in line with that view, their intentions, aims, wishes, and choices all lead to what is likable, desirable, agreeable, beneficial, and pleasant. | T: then whatever bodily deeds he undertakes in line with that view, whatever verbal deeds… whatever mental deeds he undertakes in line with that view, whatever intentions, whatever vows, whatever determinations, whatever fabrications, all lead to what is agreeable, pleasing, charming, profitable, & easeful.
an10.104:4.6 | S: Why is that? | T: Why is that?
an10.104:4.7 | S: Because their view is good.” | T: Because the view is auspicious.”
an10.104:4.8 | P: Catutthaṁ. | T: (none)

